    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with **Jonathan Aranda** and **Lawrence Butler** anchoring the lineup as the clear top-tier plays. **Jonathan Aranda** (67.88) benefits from a favorable matchup against S. Alcantara and a move up to the #2 spot in the order, yielding a +10% SP skill bump and a +12% platoon edge. Similarly, **Lawrence Butler** (64.46) remains a high-upside play, utilizing a +13% dynamic platoon advantage to overcome a neutral park factor. While **Luis Arraez** (60.99) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (59.04) are strong, note that their scores are suppressed by a \"Wind In\" factor at their venue, which may dampen power potential; however, their ability to contribute to the AVG category remains vital for our 5x5 standing.\n\nThe primary bench decision for this rotation centered on **Geraldo Perdomo** (48.90). He came closest to cracking the starting nine, but his late-order placement (#7) and a lukewarm SP matchup against Cade Cavalli kept his efficiency score just below the threshold required to displace the high-floor options currently occupying the UTIL and OF spots. While we are currently rostering **Cal Raleigh**, his absence due to IL designation keeps him on the sidelines, further thinning our options for a late-game pivot if the lineups for **Will Smith**, **Tyler Freeman**, or **Gavin Sheets** undergo significant changes before first pitch.\n\nInvestors should monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status of **Will Smith**, **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Taylor Ward** closely. **Taylor Ward** faces a significant challenge against Gausman, resulting in a defensive score (48.72) that hinges entirely on his leadoff spot. Furthermore, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (52.83) is forced into a difficult battle against Jacob deGrom; while his talent typically earns an elite rating, the -19% SP skill penalty makes him a high-variance play today. Ensure all active status alerts are enabled, particularly for **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Drew Gilbert**, in case last-minute roster shuffling is required to address stagnant lineup spots.",
